  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "Spanish has two obligatory written contractions: al (a + el) and del (de + el). These contractions occur at all style levels whenever the prepositions a or de are followed by the masculine singular definite article el. For example, 'Quieren ir al restaurante' means 'They want to go to the restaurant,' and 'Esta es la cuenta del gas' means 'This is the gas bill.' No other contractions are written in standard Spanish, even though vowels frequently run together in speech."
    }
  ],
